Architecture: SDD

Purpose:
  Define the internal architecture of the .sdd system.
  This is the meta layer: how .sdd itself is built.

Principles:
  - Separation of concerns
  - Lazy loading
  - Token efficiency
  - Explicit references
  - No circular dependencies

Components:
  PROJECT:
    path: PROJECT.sdd
    role: Root entry point

  CASES:
    path: ./cases
    role: What needs to be built

  TEMPLATES:
    path: ./templates
    role: How to build it

  CHAINS:
    path: ./chains
    role: When and in what order

  SKILLS:
    path: ./skills
    role: Engineering rules

  PROMPTS:
    path: ./prompts
    role: Prompt intelligence

  TASKS:
    path: ./tasks
    role: Work management

  DECISIONS:
    path: ./decisions
    role: Human decisions

  STATE:
    path: ./state
    role: System state

Relationships:
  PROJECT -> CASES
  PROJECT -> TEMPLATES
  PROJECT -> CHAINS
  PROJECT -> SKILLS
  PROJECT -> PROMPTS
  PROJECT -> TASKS
  PROJECT -> DECISIONS
  PROJECT -> STATE

  CASES -> CHAINS
  CASES -> TEMPLATES
  CHAINS -> SKILLS
  PROMPTS -> TASKS
  TASKS -> STATE
  DECISIONS -> ARCHITECTURE

Rules:
  [AR1] Components MUST NOT create circular dependencies.
  [AR2] References MUST be explicit and resolvable.
  [AR3] AI MUST follow declared relationships.

Note:
  This file describes .sdd's own component graph. For code architecture
  principles applied to projects, see @principles.sdd.

State: +